7 March 1987 Wimbledon Southern Championships

A new course provided a five lap circuit for the men and two laps for the ladies which proved tough and interesting and very little traffic problem by avoiding the common. Turn out in the mens race was rather low but that was probably due to the National to be held the following week. Steyning produced much too strong a team for us to contend with and we had to lose yet another Southern title. The ladies was rather a let down for us, we had a magnificant 5 Belgrave entries, but we could only start ONE.

