14 March 1987 Ham National and Inter Counties 10m for Men and National 5kms for Ladies

This was the first senior national promoted by Belgrave for many years and thanks are expressed to all of those who responded to the call to come and help. Those that helped in some ways as timekeepers, recorders, judges, catering were all appreciated. Thanks must also go to the pupils and staff of Christ's school of Richmond for their help in distributing leaflets and helping on the day. Generally it turned out to be an excellent day and an extremely accurate course with only a minor traffic problem on one section. Unfortunately as a team we did badly. We finished a lowly 8th, well out of touch of placings, even without Paul Warburton's disqualification we would have not improved. The County Team was no better and left a lot to be desired. It does not seem that long ago that we won the McSweeney Trophy.

